+        // at 35 units/m is a 3.6 m ball, and the game re-centres it once per
+        // 20 Hz game tick while this matrix is recomposed every compositor
+        // frame from the live head. Between ticks the head therefore
+        // translates INSIDE a stale 3.6 m sphere, and a 3.6 m sphere gives
+        // real parallax for a few centimetres of motion: the sky swims at
+        // the tick rate, worst while walking. Same radius, same reason it
+        // reads as near.
